            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to wait, then the Bengali for a bench."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: কুলি",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কুলি — kuli — \"a porter\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কুলি আমার ভারী মালপত্র তুলল। kuli āmār bhārī mālpôtrô tullô. The porter lifted my heavy luggage."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "At a big station the porters wear red shirts and carry loads on the head."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কুলি (kuli) has an origin that is not settled: it is often traced to the South Indian word for wages, Tamil kūli (DEDR 1905), so that a porter is someone paid by the job."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
